<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liaoyang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xiangping</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liaoyang is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> province, north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Taizi river. As Xiangping it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> commandery and of the Gongsun warlords at the end of the Han period. It was later the Eastern Capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> and Jin dynasties, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nurhaci">Nurhaci</a>'s capital from 1621 until he moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shenyang">Shenyang</a> in 1625.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liaoyang.jpg" alt="Liaoyang" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 红烧腰果 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%BE%BD%E9%98%B3%E7%99%BD%E5%A1%94%E5%85%AC%E5%9B%AD09.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
